<title>USA: Cooper says Justice Dept. ends merger review.</title>
<headline>Cooper says Justice Dept. ends merger review.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cooper Industries Inc said on Monday that the U.S. Department of Justice has concluded its investigation of the sale of Cooper's Kirsch business to Newell Co.</p>
<p>Completion of the investigation was one of the terms toward completing a deal.</p>
<p>Kirsch manufactures and distributes drapery hardware and custom window coverings in the United States and internationally, Cooper said.</p>
<p>The companies will close the transaction as soon as certain other conditions are satisfied, which is anticipated to be in early June, Cooper said.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal have not yet been disclosed.</p>
</text>
